        <article class="card reveal" id="google-user-data">
          <h2>Google User Data — Access, Use, Storage, Sharing and Deletion</h2>
          <p><strong>Feature and authorization.</strong> Classic Academy offers an optional Google Calendar integration for scheduling Classic Academy demos, onboarding sessions, and support bookings. The integration is connected only after an authorized Classic Academy administrator chooses to connect a Google account and grants Google OAuth permission.</p>
          <p><strong>Google data and permissions accessed.</strong> For OAuth-based Calendar booking, Classic Academy requests <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.owned</code> and <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.freebusy</code>. These permissions allow Classic Academy to read free/busy availability for the configured booking calendar and to create, update, or delete Calendar events owned by the connected account. In performing those actions, Classic Academy may process calendar identifiers, free/busy time ranges, event identifiers, event titles/descriptions, start and end times, meeting links, and booking attendee information that is necessary to create or manage a requested booking.</p>
          <p><strong>How Google user data is used.</strong> Google user data is used only to provide and improve the user-facing Classic Academy booking functionality: checking whether a requested time is available, preventing booking conflicts, creating the requested Calendar event, updating or cancelling that event where necessary, maintaining booking integrity, and troubleshooting failures. Classic Academy does not use Google user data for advertising, personalized advertising, retargeting, credit decisions, lending, data-broker or information-reseller services, unrelated marketing, or creation of unrelated databases.</p>
          <p><strong>AI and machine learning.</strong> Google Workspace API data obtained through this integration is not used to develop, improve, or train generalized or non-personalized artificial-intelligence or machine-learning models.</p>
          <p><strong>Storage and protection.</strong> When OAuth is used, Classic Academy stores the Google refresh credential in encrypted form so the booking service can continue operating without requiring the administrator to sign in for every booking. Access to integration credentials is restricted to authorized server-side application processes. Google Calendar availability and event information is processed only as needed for the booking operation and related service integrity. Production connections use HTTPS/TLS in transit.</p>
          <p><strong>Sharing and transfer.</strong> Classic Academy does not sell Google user data and does not share or transfer Google user data for advertising, marketing, profiling, data brokerage, credit, lending, or generalized AI/ML training. Google user data may be disclosed only to service providers acting on Our behalf where necessary to provide or secure the user-facing booking functionality, when required by applicable law, or when the connected user has expressly authorized the disclosure. Those providers may use the data only to perform the contracted service for Classic Academy.</p>
          <p><strong>Retention and deletion.</strong> Google authorization credentials are retained only while the Calendar integration remains connected and as necessary to operate the booking feature. An authorized administrator can disconnect Google Calendar in Classic Academy, revoke Classic Academy's access from the Google Account's third-party access settings, or contact Us to request deletion of stored Google authorization credentials and related integration records. We delete or render unusable the stored integration credential after disconnection or a valid deletion request, except where a limited record must be retained to meet a legal or security obligation. Calendar events already written to the user's Google Calendar remain subject to the user's own Google Calendar controls and can be deleted there.</p>
          <p><strong>Limited Use.</strong> Classic Academy's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. If any general provision elsewhere in this Privacy Policy could be interpreted more broadly, this Google User Data section controls for data obtained through Google APIs.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card reveal">
          <h2>Retention of Your Personal Data</h2>
          <p>The Company will retain Your Personal Data only for as long as is necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Policy. We will retain and use Your Personal Data to the extent necessary to comply with Our legal obligations (for example, if We are required to retain Your data to comply with applicable laws), resolve disputes, and enforce Our legal agreements and policies.</p>
          <p>Where possible, We apply shorter retention periods and/or reduce identifiability by deleting, aggregating, or anonymizing data. Unless otherwise stated, the retention periods below are maximum periods ("up to") and We may delete or anonymize data sooner when it is no longer needed for the relevant purpose. We apply different retention periods to different categories of Personal Data based on the purpose of processing and legal obligations:</p>
          <ul>
<li>
<p>Account Information</p>
<ul>
<li>User Accounts: retained for the duration of Your Account relationship plus up to 24 months after account closure to handle any post-termination issues or resolve disputes.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p>Customer Support Data</p>
<ul>
<li>Support tickets and correspondence: up to 24 months from the date of ticket closure to resolve follow-up inquiries, track service quality, and defend against potential legal claims.</li>
<li>Chat transcripts: up to 24 months for quality assurance and staff training purposes.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p>Usage Data</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Website analytics data (cookies, IP addresses, device identifiers): up to 24 months from the date of collection, which allows us to analyze trends while respecting privacy principles.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Server logs (IP addresses, access times): up to 24 months for security monitoring and troubleshooting purposes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
          <p>Usage Data is retained in accordance with the retention periods described above, and may be retained longer only where necessary for security, fraud prevention, or legal compliance.</p>
          <p>We may retain Personal Data beyond the periods stated above for different reasons:</p>
          <ul>
<li>Legal obligation: We are required by law to retain specific data (e.g., financial records for tax authorities).</li>
<li>Legal claims: Data is necessary to establish, exercise, or defend legal claims.</li>
<li>Your explicit request: You ask Us to retain specific information.</li>
<li>Technical limitations: Data exists in backup systems that are scheduled for routine deletion.</li>
</ul>
          <p>You may request information about how long We will retain Your Personal Data by contacting Us.</p>
          <p>When retention periods expire, We securely delete or anonymize Personal Data according to the following procedures:</p>
          <ul>
<li>Deletion: Personal Data is removed from Our systems and no longer actively processed.</li>
<li>Backup retention: Residual copies may remain in encrypted backups for a limited period consistent with Our backup retention schedule and are not restored except where necessary for security, disaster recovery, or legal compliance.</li>
<li>Anonymization: In some cases, We convert Personal Data into anonymous statistical data that cannot be linked back to You. This anonymized data may be retained indefinitely for research and analytics.</li>
</ul>
        </article>

